A||||4||Richard Parnell||Carb & fuel question on left turns||||1||
Z||000000||Richard Parnell||04-24-2001||02:55 PM||||Thanks Achie Ogre, on the answer re: fuel pump running after engine shut off. Yes I do run thicker oil in my car 20-50. Hopefully that's whats' keeping the fuel pump activated longer. I also have another problem when I take a fairly good left hand turn. The oil pressure drops way down momentarily and the engines kicks like there's no gas in the line. My friend got around this with his V8 Fiero by mounting the carb facing forward. I'd rather not do this as I'd have to reconfigure the throttle cabling , etc. Any ideas about that Problem . I know on the oil pressure drop I'd have to get a special oil pan with baffles.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Richard Parnell||04-24-2001||04:37 PM||||anybody?||||reg||5
Z||000002||Raydar||04-24-2001||04:43 PM||||Richard, what kind of carb do you have?<BR>(Edelbrock, I'm thinking.) <BR>You might try raising the float level just a tad, or going to a Holley with a dual inlet, center-hung float system. (Not that I am recommending a Holley carb. Personally not too fond of 'em.)<BR>Better yet, just retrofit EFI of some sort.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Butter||04-24-2001||04:50 PM||||Richard,<BR>I have a bit of the same problem.  I have been looking for a wedge plate to go under the carb in order to level it.  Haven't found any manufactors for it yet.  You or anyone got any leads on something of this order?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||04-25-2001||10:21 AM||||Try these links... <A HREF="http://www.performance-racing.com/offenhauser_equipment1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.performance-racing.com/offenhauser_equipment1.htm</A>  <BR>(12* wedge spacer for marine applications)<BR>-or- <BR> <A HREF="http://www.holley.com/HiOctn/ProdLine/Products/Marine/FMS/FMSCA/FMSCA.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.holley.com/HiOctn/ProdLine/Products/Marine/FMS/FMSCA/FMSCA.html</A>  <BR>(7* or 12* wedge spacer for square bore. 12* for spread bore carbs. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-25-2001).]||||reg||1
